{
  "about": "What fighters say or do at the turning points of a fight (kinds: engage, crit, kill, miss, dodge, hurt, fall, flee, summon, summoned, revived): by the fighter's manner (side: company) or kind of foe (role). Most are Orsino's barks (source orsino); the narrator says one now and then, never two in one exchange, and never the same one twice in a fight.",
  "kinds": [
    "engage",
    "crit",
    "kill",
    "miss",
    "dodge",
    "hurt",
    "fall",
    "flee",
    "summon",
    "summoned",
    "revived"
  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "kill.kyr.compassionate.1",
      "when": {
        "manner": "compassionate",
        "side": "company"
      },
      "text": "{Actor} stands over the body a moment, breathing hard, and does not look pleased."
    },
    {
      "id": "miss.kyr.compassionate.1",
      "when": {
        "manner": "compassionate",
        "side": "company"
      },
      "text": "{Actor} swears under {their} breath and sets {their} feet again."
